--
--  C (i, j) = 1 / (x_i XOR y_j)  in GF(2^8),  with
--     y_j = j - 1          for j in 1 .. 72   ->  0 .. 71   (data columns)
--     x_i = 72 + i - 1     for i in 1 .. 48   ->  72 .. 119   (parity rows)
--
--  The two index sets are disjoint by construction (and K + M = 72+48 = 120 <= 256,
--  so every x_i XOR y_j is a distinct non-zero field element).  EVERY square
--  submatrix of a Cauchy matrix is invertible -- that is the property that makes
--  the erasure code MDS: ANY K surviving fragments out of N reconstruct the
--  data, with no special cases and no unlucky combinations.
--
--  Frozen and self-checked offline by tools/gen-tables.py; pasted here so there
--  is nothing to prove about its construction and a human can diff it.

